% ========================================================================
% C11 re-scoping probe control — separated design, single cadence
% ========================================================================
% Identical to probe_c11_separated_design.problem (canonical CSOK
% decomposition, three credentials, one claim each) but BOTH marked claims
% carry StaticRevocation. No cadence mismatch, so `revocation_mismatch`
% cannot fire for any reason. Expected: `Model is consistent` under
% `check -k`.
%
% Purpose: pin the separated-design probe's verdict to the cadence markers
% rather than to the CSOK decomposition itself. Before the 2026-08-05
% re-scoping the probe was INCONSISTENT and this control was consistent, so
% the difference was attributable to the mismatch; after the re-scoping both
% are consistent and the pair shows the predicate is silent on the
% prescribed remedy whatever the cadences are.
% ========================================================================

import vc_metamodel.
import revocation_mismatch.
import csok_instance.


% === Revocation-cadence markers (single cadence) ===

declare static_family, static_income.

StaticRevocation(static_family).
StaticRevocation::target(static_family, has_children_claim).
StaticRevocation(static_income).
StaticRevocation::target(static_income, earns_claim).

% Close markers
!exists(StaticRevocation::new).
!exists(DynamicRevocation::new).

% 22 nodes from csok_instance (7 DCL + 12 CSL + 3 FSL) + 2 markers
scope node = 24.
